WEBVTT

1
00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:24.150
I'll tell you, in this neighbourhood, ever since
we moved here in '78, it's been really good.

2
00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:27.650
We moved in, a really good flat.

3
00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:33.750
I worked for a long time, I was very
busy, I was at the Ministry of Energy.

4
00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:43.550
Oh yes, and the older
folk might still remember,

5
00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:46.450
because I was one of the
people who cut off their power.

6
00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:48.650
[laughs] No electricity.

7
00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:51.150
Back in the '80s, the '80s and '90s.

8
00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:56.950
Along with other colleagues, we did it so we
could keep the grid going, at least somehow.

9
00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:01.150
As you can see, a lot
got built in that period.

10
00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:04.789
Industry, and… there was building.

11
00:01:04.839 --> 00:01:07.250
A great deal was built.

12
00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:13.150
Plus the power grid we still have
today; that was built back then too.

13
00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:18.750
And in the '50s and '60s they built Romania's
first big hydroelectric dam, at Bicaz.

14
00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:26.250
There were Russians involved too, yes,
but our people built everything as well.

15
00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:31.550
Back then, the power grid
was built by our own people.

16
00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:43.050
And these blocks went up too. The whole
area was built in the '70s and '80s.

17
00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:44.450
But who built the blocks here?

18
00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:49.650
IDEB did, IDEB Bucharest.

19
00:01:51.500 --> 00:02:00.152
IDEB Bucharest had its headquarters right
here too, across from Piața 1 Mai, where

20
00:02:00.202 --> 00:02:01.850
Enel used to be.

21
00:02:01.900 --> 00:02:05.250
Where that building is? Yes,
that was IDEB Bucharest,

22
00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:08.050
the Bucharest Electricity
Distribution Company.

23
00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:15.650
They built these blocks, and with the Ministry
of Energy they built more over that way too.

24
00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:25.050
And after I retired, I
got around a lot by bike.

25
00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:35.050
Practically every day I'd set off
from here and ride to Herăstrău Park.

26
00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:38.050
Really pleasant, as you can imagine.

27
00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:47.450
And on the way to Herăstrău,
at one point, I bumped into…

28
00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:52.965
you won't believe it, Simona
Halep, if you've heard of her.

29
00:02:53.015 --> 00:02:56.050
She was cycling to Herăstrău too.

30
00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:06.650
A lot of the old residents have moved
away, and new people have come and bought.

31
00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:12.050
After we moved here, you can't imagine
the New Year's Eve parties we had!

32
00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:17.850
We'd stay home, we didn't go anywhere,
we'd throw them at home with the kids,

33
00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:20.850
because I've got quite a
big family, four children.

34
00:03:23.900 --> 00:03:25.850
The eldest is retired himself now.

